discussion_comments.comment_body:
I would suggest using the default mime types if there were no mime types specified.

```ts
let mimeType: string | undefined = undefined
if (options.mime) {
  mimeType = getMimeType(path, options.mime) ?? getMimeType(path)
} else {
  mimeType = getMimeType(path)
}
```

Yeah, sometimes TypeScript can be troublesome.

In this case, it's preferable to keep backward compatibility with my implementation. I believe using `options!.env!` or `options?.env?` isn't too hacky. It simply translates to:

```ts
if (options && options.env) {
  //...
}
```

But thank you for the suggestion!

